{"id": "EUVD-2026-60109", "enisaUuid": "a45b9fa8-99d5-33c5-9566-89dc590b3656", "description": "openssl_encrypt versions before 1.4.0 contain an authentication bypass vulnerability in CamelliaCipher that disables HMAC tag generation and verification when the PYTEST_CURRENT_TEST environment variable is set. Attackers with code execution can set this environment variable to produce unauthenticated ciphertext and bypass integrity protection on encrypted data.", "datePublished": "2026-08-17T11:04:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T15:21:00", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/jahlives/openssl_encrypt/security/advisories/GHSA-rvc2-5jxq-gpcj", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openssl-encrypt-before-hmac-authentication-bypass-via-environment-variable"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8p4p-w6mq-4grq", "CVE-2026-74890", "PYSEC-2026-3766"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0eb08968-5a11-31ab-a6bd-727eb384decf", "product": {"name": "openssl_encrypt", "vendor": {"name": "jahlives"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.4.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "26944d92-e6b2-3f5a-87f9-788a4a6186fd", "vendor": {"name": "jahlives"}}], "isExploited": false}